            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "hi, i'd like to work on this.\n\ni'd reproduce the `foo(one, two)` / `baz(five, six)` case first. then i'd try your untested idea: end each preview refresh with one more dry-run of the span at the primary's own session start, so shared state is last written for the primary.\n\nthe other cursors already look right, and therefore this would only be about putting the primary's history back last. but does that dry-run need to replay the whole span, or is restoring `_select`'s parent-child history enough for this ticket?\r\n",
